   "en": "The Gemara clarifies why this principle might have applied here. «And what mitzva» is there in hearing the reading of the High Priest? It is a fulfillment of the principle expressed in the verse: «“The king’s glory is in the multitude of people”» (Proverbs 14:28). Having a large assembly involved in a mitzva gives honor to God. Therefore, the mishna «teaches us» that the problem with seeing both events was only a practical one."
